---
title: "Flow 4 — Login (matches AuthService.java — no Redis, no WebSocket; JwtAuthFilter is stateless, never reads user_sessions back)"
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant Client as Angular SPA
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant IAM as Identity and Access

    User->>Client: Enter email + password, click "Log In"
    Client->>GW: POST /api/identity/auth/login {email, password}
    GW->>IAM: forward (StripPrefix=2 — IAM sees POST /auth/login)

    IAM->>IAM: look up user by email (soft-delete aware)
    IAM->>IAM: verify password hash (BCrypt via PasswordEncoder)

    alt wrong credentials
        IAM-->>GW: 401 InvalidCredentialsException
        GW-->>Client: login failed
        Client-->>User: "Incorrect email or password"
    else credentials valid, but account not ACTIVE
        IAM-->>GW: 403 AccountNotActiveException
        GW-->>Client: account disabled
        Client-->>User: "This account is inactive — contact an administrator"
    else credentials valid and account ACTIVE
        IAM->>IAM: resolve the user's role-scope-assignment claims<br/>(AssignmentService.resolveClaimsForUser)
        IAM->>IAM: JwtService issues JWT — sub, email, role (flat legacy kind),<br/>assignments, iat, exp
        IAM->>IAM: persist UserSession — user_id, token_hash<br/>(SHA-256 of the JWT, base64), expires_at, created_at<br/>(audit/revocation bookkeeping — written but not read back by anything today)
        IAM-->>GW: 200 {token, role, name}
        GW-->>Client: store token
        Client-->>User: redirected to role dashboard
    end

    Note over GW,IAM: No Redis, no WebSocket anywhere in this real flow.<br/>Every later request's auth check (JwtAuthFilter) validates the JWT<br/>signature and expiry purely statelessly — it does not look up<br/>user_sessions or any cache on each request.
